<libraries>
<library name="Cinch_108-0904-001_Banana_Jack_v2">
<description>&lt;b&gt;Cinch 108-0904-001 banana jack&lt;/b&gt;&lt;p&gt;
Custom PCB mounting footprint based on the Cinch drawing supplied by the user. The mechanical mounting cutout is implemented as a simple 8.5 mm non-plated round hole (slightly larger than the 8.33 mm nominal keyed panel cutout) for easy PCB fabrication. A 3.5 x 3.5 mm solder pad is placed on the BOTTOM side adjacent to the hole so the jack's rear solder lug can be connected with a short bodge wire.&lt;p&gt;
Component origin = center of mounting hole. Bottom-side solder pad center is 9.50 mm to the right of the mounting-hole center, moving the entire pad outside the retaining-nut area for easy soldering.&lt;p&gt;
The silkscreen circle represents the approximate 11.13 mm front-body diameter. Verify mechanical clearances against the actual hardware before fabrication.
</description>
<packages>
<package name="CINCH_108-0904-001_BODGE">
<description>&lt;b&gt;Cinch 108-0904-001, custom PCB mount&lt;/b&gt;&lt;p&gt;
8.5 mm NPTH mounting hole plus one bottom-side 3.5 mm square electrical solder pad. Pad 1 is intentionally separate from the mechanical hole; connect the jack's solder lug to Pad 1 with a short wire.
</description>
<hole x="0" y="0" drill="8.5"/>
